#: src/input-files.md:1
msgid "Input Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:3
msgid ""
"Input files can be provided with `[cache(inputs = FILES)]`, where `FILES` is "
"an expression that is evaluated with recipe arguments in scope and whose "
"evaluated elements are paths. Paths may be absolute or relative to the "
"recipe’s working directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:8
msgid ""
"Each input file is hashed with BLAKE3 and added to the `inputs` cache key, "
"which contains a map of paths to hashes."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:11
msgid ""
"Any changes to the contents of an input file changes the cache key, which "
"causes the next invocation to miss the cache and re-run."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:14
msgid "Missing inputs and paths to directories are errors."
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:16
msgid ""
"In this example, the `build` recipe will re-run if `lib.c` or `main.c` "
"change:"
msgstr ""

#: src/input-files.md:18
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"set unstable\n"
"set lists\n"
"\n"
"[script]\n"
"[cache(inputs = [\"lib.c\", \"main.c\"])]\n"
"build:\n"
"  cc lib.c main.c -o main\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
